<title>BELGIUM: EU, Council strike deal on interconnections directive.</title>
<headline>EU, Council strike deal on interconnections directive.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament and the Council of Ministers struck a deal early on Thursday on a key telecommunications liberalisation measure -- the draft directive on interconnections.</p>
<p>A conciliation committee agreed a compromise on the text, COM(95)379, just after midnight after five hours of discussions, a Council official said.</p>
<p>The legislation sets out rules to ensure that phone companies can connect their networks under fair terms once the EU's telecommunications market is fully opened to competition.</p>
<p>The official said details of the accord would be available later on Thursday.</p>
</text>
